{
  "spec": "druid-restoration",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Restoration druid healer rotation (stage 2 of the healer build), written against the fork's fake raid: the healer is raid player 0, the four fake party members are players 1 to 4 and the tank is player 5. The tank carries Regrowth and Rejuvenation for the whole fight (Nature's Splendor makes them 27 and 15 seconds), Healing Touch fires only on a real hole in his health bar and only while the mana bar is above the share of the fight left, so the mana lasts instead of running out at the first long fight. Party members get Wild Growth when two are hurt, Rejuvenation when one is, Tranquility when two are well down. Nature's Swiftness is cast by hand and always with an instant Healing Touch under 35% tank health, the major-cooldown pass is told to leave it alone for a healer. Top ranks only, on purpose: the site rewrites every ranked id in a rotation to the highest rank the character has learned, so a downranked heal could not survive it. Healing Touch rank 11 and Rejuvenation rank 11 are Ahn'Qiraj book ranks (core.IncludeAQ is false), so the top ranks are 10; the client's second Regrowth and Rejuvenation ids (436937-436946, 417057-417068) are not taught by the trainer and are not used.",
  "expected_idle": [
    {
      "id": 1238215,
      "reason": "Wild Growth is paced like Healing Touch: it waits until the mana bar is 20 percent above the share of the fight still to come. The ladder's healer wears nothing, so its small pool goes to the tank's Regrowth and Rejuvenation first and never gets that far ahead, and it casts none in the ladder's runs. A geared healer does: it casts Wild Growth once or twice in a 180 second fight of the fork's healsim test profile (sim/druid/restoration, with 700 healing power)."
    }
  ],
